# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_config_recall.py" "CONFIG RECALL GATE: PASS" "config-coupling recall preservation + data-dump skip correctly scoped (recall-safe + precision)" "config-coupling recall lock for the PR #339 data-dump skip: _cg_config._is_data_dump_file SKIPS data-dump / fixture / seed / locale files at config MINT time (their keys are model FIELD NAMES or i18n message ids, not a shared app-config resource -- audit: 65-91 percent of config couples on real Django/Rails repos were these fixture-field-name FALSE couples) and #339 raised the per-file distinct-key cap 500 -> 2000. An OVER-SKIP audit (MEASURED on crafted repos mirroring build_graph's wiring _iter_config_files + _iter_source_files -> _config_graph) found NO real over-skip dropping genuine coupling: (a) the PATH-SEGMENT signals (fixtures/ seeds/ locales/) are load-bearing for the #339 precision gain -- narrowing them re-admits the field-name flood; (b) gating the BASENAME signals (*_data.json / dump*) on content-shape rescued 1 real couple but RE-ADMITTED a keyed-object dump's shipping_address false couple (measured tradeoff), so the basename signal is correctly precision-biased; (c) the CONTENT-SHAPE array-of-objects probe loses ZERO recall on genuine array configs because a real array config exposes only generic field NAMES as keys and the real identifiers are VALUES the content-free extractor never reads -- while disabling it re-couples an un-named row dump's customer_billing_email (measured), so it earns its keep. NO change was made to _cg_config.py; this gate FREEZES the measured behaviour so a future rescue-a-config-out-of-a-dump-path narrowing cannot silently re-admit the #339 flood. Proven offline (no Postgres), content-free (key NAMES + paths only): (R1) a real key/value OBJECT config couples its two readers via a SPECIFIC key; (R2) a 2100-key GENUINE config (> the 2000 per-file cap) still couples on an early specific key (the cap truncates only a tail -- #339 raised it from 500 because discourse site_settings.yml has 1061 real keys); (P1) a Django fixture under fixtures/ mints NO key so a shared field name does NOT couple; (P2) an UN-NAMED array-of-objects row dump caught only by content-shape stays skipped; (P3) a locale tree message id does NOT couple; (REC-SCOPE) a real OBJECT config is never caught by the content probe while an array-of-objects dump is; (NC) _is_data_dump_file degrades any malformed / oversized / binary input to a bool, never raises" "config recall: the #339 data-dump/fixture/seed/locale skip is recall-safe AND correctly scoped -- a real key/value config still couples its readers (incl. a >2000-key genuine config past the per-file cap), while fixture-field-name / row-dump / locale-message-id false couples stay gone; the audit found no safe narrowing (every rescue re-admits the measured 65-91 percent #339 flood), so the behaviour is frozen unchanged and content-free" 28
